[
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__job_status",
    "description": "Read one Slurm job's status by job id (digits only).

Answers found: false when the id is well formed but not in the
queue; a malformed id is refused before Slurm is touched.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__job_status(args: { job_id: string; }): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__submit_job",
    "description": "Submit the run's guarded batch script to Slurm; answers the job id.

Directives are scheduler sizing only — partition, time, mem, ntasks,
cpus-per-task, gres — each inside a ceiling; the job name (the
per-user theta- prefix), the log paths, and the script body are
gateway-forced. This spends cluster time: the theta side confirms
it before the call leaves.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__submit_job(args: { directives?: { [key: string]: string | number; } | null; run_name: string; }): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__cancel_job",
    "description": "Cancel one gateway-owned job (the theta- prefix marks ownership).

Only jobs whose name carries this user's theta-<user>- prefix are
cancelled; anything else is refused. Answers found: false when the
queue no longer holds the id — nothing to cancel, not an error.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__cancel_job(args: { job_id: string; }): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__job_logs",
    "description": "Read one job's stdout and stderr from its run directory.

Returns the last tail_lines of each (100 by default, 1000 at most).
Answers found: false when no run in the staging tree holds a log
for the id — a job that never started, or not a gateway job.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__job_logs(args: {
  job_id: string;
  // @integer
  tail_lines?: number | null;
}): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__list_environments",
    "description": "List the cluster's partition-state groups: where a job can run.

Returns one record per sinfo partition-state group — partition name,
whether it is the default, availability, time limit, node count,
state, and node list.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__list_environments(args: {}): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__fetch_artifacts",
    "description": "Fetch one run's files back in-band: the whole run directory by
default, or the named picks.

The answer is whole or not at all — every file is read and sized
within the in-band cap before anything returns. Past the cap the
refusal names the out-of-band path: scp from the run directory on
the cluster.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__fetch_artifacts(args: { paths?: Array<string> | null; run_name: string; }): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  },
  {
    "name": "mcp__theta_compute__stage_files",
    "description": "Stage input files into one run's directory under the staging root.

Files travel in-band as base64 (32 MiB per call by default) and the
path sandbox confines them to the run directory. Past the cap the
refusal names the out-of-band path: scp to the run directory on the
cluster. Staging lands whole or not at all.

codemode tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__theta_compute__stage_files(args: { files: Array<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>; run_name: string; }): Promise<{ content: Array<{ data?: string; mimeType?: string; text?: string; type: "text" | "image" | "audio" | "resource_link" | "resource"; [key: string]: unknown; }>; isError?: boolean; structuredContent?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; [key: string]: unknown; }>; };
```"
  }
]

